  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "MqttClient_HandlePacket",
    "file": "wolfmqtt/src/mqtt_client.c",
    "description": "In the MQTT_PACKET_TYPE_PUBLISH path, MqttClient_HandlePacket unconditionally calls MqttProps_Free(publish->props) after payload processing, but does not validate that publish->props points to a valid MqttProp list allocated/initialized by the decoder. With fuzzed packet/state data, publish->props can be attacker-controlled garbage, so MqttProps_Free walks and writes through an invalid pointer (head->type = MQTT_PROP_NONE), causing the SEGV seen in mqtt_packet.c:1902.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires reaching MqttClient_Subscribe -> MqttClient_WaitType -> MqttClient_HandlePacket with an incoming packet interpreted as PUBLISH under v5 property handling, and having publish->props set to a non-NULL invalid pointer (e.g., malformed/partial decode or corrupted packet object state from crafted input). When HandlePacket finishes reading payload, it frees props without pointer/list integrity checks, leading to invalid write in MqttProps_Free."
  },
